"Aha!," I said, "A new score list!". And so came the Valkyrie ascension 
after only a few attempts. I think I've got this game down to a science 
now. Even for a valkyrie, I learned a few things to tune my game. The 
details are at the bottom of the post.

This was a harder ascension than I'm used to for a valkyrie. Only 6 
wishes, and only 1 magic marker. No scroll of genocide. No Ludios. No 
magic lamp. Still, perserverance eventually paid off. Probably could 
have improved my wishes by 1) clearing the dragons from the castle 
before wishing (gray dragon dropped scales after I'd wished for the 
armor) and 2) attempting the quest before the castle - my AC was in the 
-20s from a coaligned priest and got "oR from Sokoban. (found speed 
boots on Home 2). Found a bag of holding early, however, so that was a 
big help.

Asmodeus, Juiblex, Baalzebub and Orcus all went down without incident. 
  A well-placed trapdoor was about the only incident in Gehennom, 
forcing me to pick-axe through nearly the entire level looking for the 
upstairs. =oC through the zoo in the wizard's tower, and /oD to deal 
with Rodney. =oC through the Sanctum, ran through the pick-axed 
labyrinths of Gehennom, and into the planes. I'd used potions of full 
healing to get up to around 250hp, so I wasn't too worried (and had 2 
"oLS!). A ?oC I'd found was used to recharge the OoF, so I didn't spend 
much time wandering about. First altar was the correct one.

I'm really working on the speed now -- 30k turns is quite a bit shorter 
than previous ascensions. Also realizing that I don't need to be a 
packrat. Clearly not everything is required to make a successful kit. 
Less things hauled means more room for loot :-D

First genocideless ascension for me (I think!) I got lucky with the 
arch-lich, who could have easily finished me off as I hadn't found my 
"oLS yet. But, it kept trying the touch of death, and neither his 
monster summoning or cursing abilities were able to kill me. /oD kept 
most of the master mind flayers away, and I found a can of grease deep 
in Gehennom to deal with that particular threat.

Also, no polypiling as I failed to find a /oP. Again, first time I've 
stuck to that particular challenge.

